Trajectory files from new runs: 

- Ra has been increased from MacMillan et al. 2022 from 9e6 to 1e8
- Case numbering: 
case0 = unladen (trajectories are tracers)
- Each case has a *.mat file which contains a single Matlab cell called "trajectories" and is of size Nx1, where N is the number of individual trajectories recorded. Note that this only includes a subset of the total number of trajectories in the simulation (i.e. does not include all of them). 
- Each cell entry (e.g. trajectories{1}) contains a Nt x 14 array, where Nt is the number of time steps that that particle lived for. Nt is not necessarily the same across droplets because they live for different amounts of time
- Each droplet has 14 pieces of data recorded along its lifetime, and the columns are given below:

Col1: Ignore	
Col2: Time
Col3: xp
Col4: yp
Col5: zp
Col6: vpx
Col7: vpy
Col8: vpz
Col9: radius
Col10: Tp
Col11: Tf (fluid temp interpolated to particle location)
Col12: qf (fluid vapor mixing ratio interpolated to particle location)
Col13: q* (vapor mixing ratio at droplet surface, including curvature and solute effects)
Col14: RH (air relative humidity interpolated to droplet location)
